      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/animus/{size}/1887_2.png",
      "created_at": "2016-04-26T01:18:59.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>I don't know what you have, so I'm just going to throw some suggestions out there:</p><p>- Bottom of the 9th</p><p>- Pandemic (and lots of co-ops): You can play this solo using two characters, and as a matter of fact I have.</p><p>&nbsp;- The D&amp;D dungeoncrawls in a box (Wrath of Ashardalon, Castle Ravenloft, Legend of Drizzt, Temple of Elemental Evil): Plays 1-5 players.</p><p>- Legendary Deckbuilding games: They're a pain to sort in cleanup, but any of them are good (Marvel, Alien, Predator)</p><p>- Robinson Crusoe: Can be played pretty well as a solo worker placement game. It is brutal, but tells an engaging story.&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
