      "id": 174354,
      "name": "Phantom5613",
      "username": "Phantom5613",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantom5613/{size}/1906_2.png",
      "created_at": "2016-05-09T06:07:19.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>If you can get at least 3-4 people to play with, I can always recomend The Red Dragon Inn, a game that's something like a grown-up version of Munchkin.</p><p>It's a game where all the players are characters from a D&amp;D style dungeoneering party that have rested up and are now partying at the Red Dragon Inn(hence the name). There the players gamble, rough-house and drink, all the while trying their best to get eachother's share of treasure from the previous adventure.</p><p>What's great about this game is that there's so many different character's/decks that you can play, each unique! It verges on Sentinel's levels of variation! I'd start with the base set; it has a human female fighter(Fiona the Volitile), an elf preistess(Deirdre the Preistess), a halfling rouge(Gerki the Sneak), and a elderly human wizard with his Monty Python-esque rabbit familiar(Zot the Wizard and Pooky).</p><p>As far as I know there are at least 5 base sets to get with a mess of single deck expansions, but even one 4-deck set is enough to have quite the time with friends!</p>",
      "post_number": 12,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:57:42.213Z",
